      <h2 id="article-heading">URL Encoding Specification &amp; Mode Comparison</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7;">RFC 3986 specifies percent-encoding to represent characters in URIs outside the allowed ASCII character set. Understanding the distinction between component and full URI modes prevents broken routes and corrupted parameters.</p>

