    <!-- Common Mistakes Section -->
    <section style="margin: 2.5rem 0;" aria-labelledby="mistakes-heading">
      <h2 id="mistakes-heading">Common URL Encoding Mistakes</h2>
      <ul style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8; margin-left: 1.25rem;">
        <li><strong>Double-Encoding:</strong> Encoding an already percent-encoded string converts existing <code>%</code> characters into <code>%25</code> (e.g. <code>%20</code> becomes <code>%2520</code>). Always verify whether incoming data is already encoded before applying transformation.</li>
        <li><strong>Using encodeURI for Query Values:</strong> Running <code>encodeURI</code> on a parameter value leaves characters like <code>&amp;</code> and <code>+</code> unencoded, causing server parsers to truncate or split values unexpectedly.</li>
        <li><strong>Malformed Percent Sequences:</strong> Decoding a string with a bare percent sign (such as <code>discount=50%</code> instead of <code>discount=50%25</code>) throws a fatal JavaScript <code>URIError: URI malformed</code>. Safe tools catch and surface this error clearly.</li>
      </ul>
